"""Source-grounded teaching notes for send commands and polling support."""
from lesson_writer import author,CPP
PREFIX='src/org/minima/system/commands/'
LIMIT='The command counterpart is absent and parity remains not_verified. This is an authored source lesson and a proposed verification design, not evidence that this command is implemented or that its tests pass.'
ADAPT='No native command counterpart exists. A future port should retain the pinned Command/CommandRunner parsing and reply model and reuse compatible transaction, JSON and stream primitives. Required wallet/database/miner bindings and failure ordering must be implemented explicitly. Java command strings here are executable parser input, so quoting, separators and ignored child statuses are observable behavior.'
def lesson(name,purpose,steps,tests,exercise,adaptation=ADAPT):
 author(PREFIX+'send/'+name+'.md',purpose,steps,adaptation,lambda link:'No direct command parity experiment was found in the inspected harnesses. Proposed future test: '+tests+' This experiment has not been implemented or run for this lesson; constituent codec or runner tests do not establish command coverage.',exercise,LIMIT)
lesson('sendpoll','Manage a queue of send command strings through add, list and remove actions.',[
 'Obtain the polling manager from Main even for an unknown action. The default action is add.',
 'For add, take the original complete command and replace the first occurrence of sendpoll with send. Reject only the exact resulting string send; do not execute or validate the resulting send command here.',
 'Queue the transformed text and return it as response.command. An explicit action:add remains in that text; the UID is generated inside the polling manager.',
 'For list, serialize copied SendPollMessage entries in queue order and report total. For remove, require a UID, request its removal and report that UID regardless of whether it existed.',
 'An unknown action returns the otherwise successful reply with an empty response. Accepted parameter names mirror the send wrapper and do not themselves guarantee eventual send success.'
], 'Capture manager calls and exact strings for bare sendpoll, trailing spaces, action:add, quoted values and repeated occurrences of the word. Compare empty/duplicate queues, unknown removal and unknown action replies. Do not execute queued transfers.', 'Why can add accept a command that the polling worker will later reject?')
lesson('sendview','Read a serialized TxPoW transaction file and return its JSON for inspection.',[
 'Require file and resolve it through MiniFile.createBaseFile, then read the complete byte array.',
 'Wrap bytes as MiniData and decode using TxPoW.convertMiniDataVersion.',
 'Return response.txpow as the decoded object’s JSON. The unused local response object has no effect.',
 'The method does not explicitly recalculate the TxPoW ID, add signatures or call a miner. File and decoding failures escape to the command framework.'
], 'Use fixed signed and unsigned TxPoW files, missing paths, directories and truncated bytes; compare nested JSON and errors. Verify that wallet/miner receivers are untouched and isolate any ID recalculation inside the decoder from this method’s own statements.', 'Which operation determines whether a malformed file reaches toJSON?')
lesson('sendpost','Read a TxPoW file, calculate its ID and hand it to asynchronous mining.',[
 'Resolve/read the required file and decode its complete bytes as a TxPoW.',
 'Call calculateTXPOWID before constructing the reply.',
 'Place the object JSON under response.txpow, then call mineTxPoWAsync with that same object.',
 'Return only if the miner call returns. This method has no direct signature-validation or MMR-age check; downstream components determine acceptance.'
], 'Decode a deterministic file and capture miner argument identity plus its recalculated ID/JSON. Inject decoding and miner failures, checking that no earlier failure calls mining. Use a recording miner, not live submission.', 'Why is the help text’s approximate proof-validity window not an implemented age check in this file?')
lesson('sendsign','Add wallet script proofs and signatures to both transactions in an exported TxPoW, then write a new signed file.',[
 'Read/decode the required TxPoW file before looking up Wallet. If a password is present and the seed is unavailable, unlock and remember to relock later.',
 'Visit ordinary transaction inputs in order. Resolve each address to a wallet script row, reject a missing row, append its ScriptProof and sign the transaction ID with that row’s public key.',
 'Repeat for burn-transaction inputs using the burn witness and burn transaction ID. The reqsigs list is checked but never populated: repeated public keys are signed again for each input.',
 'Relock only after both loops complete, recalculate the TxPoW ID and write signedtransaction-<time>.txn in the base folder.',
 'Return the absolute output filename under response.txpow. Relocking is not in finally; an earlier signing/script failure can bypass it. The demo main merely prints MiniData encodings of 0 through 511.'
], 'Use two ordinary inputs sharing one key and a burn input with the same key; record three signing calls and which transaction ID each receives. Compare appended proofs/signatures and output bytes. Inject missing script/signing/file-write failures and capture unlock/relock ordering with a fake vault.', 'Why would adding pubkey to reqsigs fix a likely intention but break a literal translation?')
lesson('wallet/createfrom','Build and export an unsigned custom transaction by orchestrating existing txn commands.',[
 'Parse source/destination addresses, amount, token ID, burn and script. Positive burn is rejected for a non-Minima token.',
 'Generate a 32-byte random ID and invoke txncreate, then txnaddamount with source, recipient, amount and burn.',
 'Only txnaddamount status is checked explicitly. On false, invoke txndelete and throw its error.',
 'Invoke txnscript with a constructed JSON string, txnmmr, then txnexport showtxn:true and txndelete. Copy export.response into the outer reply.',
 'The local runCommand helper always invokes runMultiCommand and takes element zero. Other child statuses are ignored and cleanup is not guaranteed on thrown exceptions.'
], 'A scripted recording runner should compare exact command text and source order, random-ID reuse, positive token-burn rejection and cleanup after txnaddamount false. Inject false statuses versus thrown exceptions at each later step to distinguish returned failure from aborted cleanup.', 'If txnscript returns status:false, does this wrapper stop before exporting?')
lesson('wallet/constructfrom','Construct an unsigned custom transaction from an explicit comma-separated input list and specified payment/change outputs.',[
 'Require coinlist, script, recipient address/amount and change address/amount; changeaddress is parsed even when no change output will be made.',
 'Create a random custom-transaction ID. StringTokenizer splits coinlist on commas and discards empty tokens; trim each surviving coin ID and invoke txninput.',
 'Check each input command’s status. A false result deletes the row then throws its error.',
 'Invoke the payment output and add change only for a strictly positive change amount. Their statuses are not checked here.',
 'Attach the script, request MMR proofs, export with showtxn:true, delete the row and return the export response. The first result from each runMultiCommand is selected.'
], 'Capture command traces for repeated/empty/whitespace input tokens, nonpositive change and invalid change address. Inject one failed input versus a failed output to show the different cleanup/continuation rules. Compare resulting exported transactions only after child commands are bound.', 'For coinlist A,, B, which txninput calls are created?')
lesson('wallet/postfrom','Import a serialized TxnRow into the custom transaction database and post it through txnpost.',[
 'Look up TxnDB before parsing required data, then decode a TxnRow. If id is present, replace its ID, although id is absent from getValidParams and normal validation may reject it first.',
 'Read mmr, retain the row ID and add the complete row to the database. Parse mine only after insertion.',
 'When mmr is true, invoke txnmmr; then invoke txnpost with mine, followed by txndelete.',
 'Copy txnpost.response into the outer reply without checking its status. A thrown exception before deletion leaves the inserted row; a false status can still be followed by deletion.'
], 'Use a fake TxnDB and recording runner to observe insertion before malformed mine, ID collision/replacement and optional proof rebuilding. Test id through the public runner separately from direct invocation because their validation paths differ. Compare post false versus thrown exception cleanup.', 'Which stored object remains if parsing mine fails after addCompleteTransaction?')
lesson('wallet/signfrom','Import a TxnRow, sign with an explicitly supplied private key/use count, optionally post, and export the result.',[
 'Look up the custom database, decode data, optionally replace ID and insert the complete row before parsing privatekey/keyuses/post.',
 'Invoke txnsign with publickey:custom. With post=true append txnpostauto:true and txnpostmine:true to that signing command.',
 'Invoke txnexport, then txndelete, without first checking sign or export status.',
 'Take the export response object and add post. For post=true, try to copy txpow from signres.response; an exception in this small extraction block is logged and swallowed.',
 'Return the modified export response. Failures before deletion can retain the row; failures extracting the export response happen after deletion. The private key is parser text passed to the existing signer, not handled by a new signing algorithm here.'
], 'Record command strings/row identity and parse failure order using synthetic keys. Vary sign status, export response type and missing posted TxPoW; compare whether the wrapper throws, logs or returns. A later integration fixture must verify actual signatures and key-use accounting.', 'Does post:true prove that posting succeeded, or only record the requested option?')
lesson('wallet/sendfrom','Orchestrate an addressed transfer signed by a caller-supplied private key and key-use count.',[
 'Parse addresses, amount, token and burn; reject positive burn for a non-Minima token. Read script, key, uses, mine (default true) and split.',
 'Attempt to parse optional state, swallowing any exception and treating malformed state as absent.',
 'Create a random row and run txnaddamount including split/burn/fromaddress. A false status deletes the row and throws.',
 'Attach the script. For each state key, parse its numeric port and construct StateVariable, then inject its normalized port/data into a quoted txnstate command.',
 'Run txnmmr, custom txnsign and txnpost, then txndelete. Unlike several sibling wrappers, check txnpost.status after deletion and throw its error on false.',
 'Other child statuses are not explicitly checked. Exceptions can skip deletion; no try/finally transaction or private-key lifetime policy is added by this file.'
], 'Capture malformed-state suppression, ordered state commands, split propagation, default synchronous mining and source-address text. Inject txnaddamount failure and txnpost false to verify both cleanup points; inject an exception in state parsing after row creation to expose retained state.', 'How do malformed JSON state and a valid state object with an invalid numeric key follow different paths?')
lesson('wallet/rawfrom','Provide the deprecated unsigned transaction builder whose input objects each carry a coin ID and script.',[
 'Parse input/output arrays and optional state before allocating a random custom-transaction row.',
 'For each input object, read string coinid/script and invoke txninput followed immediately by txnscript. Input order therefore also determines script-command order.',
 'For each output object, require string address/amount, default tokenid to 0x00 and storestate to true, then invoke txnoutput.',
 'Convert each state key to an integer port, stringify its value with Java concatenation and use StateVariable normalization before invoking txnstate.',
 'Export with showtxn:true and delete the row. No txnmmr, signing or posting is performed here. Child statuses are ignored, and an exception can skip deletion.'
], 'Compare exact traces for two inputs with different scripts, omitted output defaults, wrong JSON types, Unicode/quoted script text and numeric/null state values. Verify absence of an MMR command. Exercise a child false status separately from an exception.', 'Why can replacing this with rawtxnfrom change command ordering even when the exported transaction looks similar?')
lesson('wallet/rawtxnfrom','Build an unsigned transaction with separate arrays for input coin IDs, output objects and scripts.',[
 'Require inputs, outputs and scripts arrays; parse optional state before creating a random transaction row.',
 'Read each input as a string coin ID and issue txninput for all inputs first.',
 'Read output address/amount strings, apply tokenid=0x00 and storestate=true defaults, then issue each txnoutput.',
 'Only after all outputs, issue txnscript for each script string. Convert optional state entries through integer ports and StateVariable, then issue txnstate.',
 'Export with showtxn:true, delete and return export.response. There is no explicit proof-building/signing/posting command or child-status check. The inherited help example still shows the older rawfrom input-object format.'
], 'Use a runner trace to distinguish all-inputs/all-outputs/all-scripts ordering from rawfrom. Test a stale help-shaped input object (which should fail its string cast), empty arrays, output defaults and a child command returning false. Future end-to-end tests should compare TxnRow bytes.', 'At what stage does this implementation reject an object in the inputs array, and has txncreate already run?')
lesson('wallet/createtokenfrom','Create a token output funded from one source address, then prove, sign and post the custom transaction.',[
 'Parse funding address, requested amount, script and custom key/use count. Name may be an object, which must contain name, or a plain string wrapped in an object.',
 'Decimals defaults to eight. The explicit check rejects values above sixteen but has no lower-bound check. Floor the requested supply and require it to be greater than zero and no more than one trillion.',
 'Compute backing Minima as MINI_UNIT multiplied by 10^decimals and floored supply; scale is MAX_DECIMAL_PLACES minus decimals.',
 'Create a row and txnaddamount from the source back to itself. A false status deletes and throws. Construct a TOKENID_CREATE output with storestate=true and a Token carrying the name JSON and fixed RETURN TRUE token script.',
 'Retrieve the live row’s transaction and replace output zero with that token output, retaining any change output. Then attach the funding script, build MMR proofs, sign with the custom key and post.',
 'Delete before checking final post.status; false becomes a command exception. Intermediate child statuses and thrown-error cleanup are not consistently handled.'
], 'Compare supply flooring and backing arithmetic for decimals 0/8/16/17/negative, missing JSON name and boundary supplies. Record output-zero replacement and retained change, plus signing/post command order. Use fake signer/miner receivers until real token-creation consensus parity is available.', 'What supply is actually created for amount 2.9, and which value enters the backing calculation?')
lesson('wallet/consolidatefrom','Collect mature coins from one address and redistribute their total, with a separate helper that produces a single output.',[
 'Parse source/token/maxcoins (default 50), burn and custom signing data; positive token burn is rejected by the command path. Create the temporary row before searching the current chain.',
 'Search source/token coins, sort descending by raw amount, reject coins younger than three blocks or present in mempool, and fail if none remain. This filter does not call the miner’s pending-coin check.',
 'Iterate valid coins, add their token-scaled amounts and invoke txninput. The counter starts at one and is incremented before comparing >maxcoins after insertion, so maxcoins zero or negative still admits one coin.',
 'For Minima and positive burn, require burn strictly less than total and subtract it; otherwise delete and throw. Emit ten equal total/10 outputs to the source address.',
 'Attach script/proofs, sign, post with mine (default true), delete and return response without checking final status. Failed child input/output statuses are also ignored.',
 'createConsolidate is a distinct public helper: it takes all supplied coins without age/count filtering, subtracts any positive burn regardless of token, emits one output, always uses mine:true and returns the child response.'
], 'Use ordered synthetic coins to check age-three boundary, mempool exclusion, descending selection and maxcoins -1/0/1/50. Compare ten outputs in runCommand against one in createConsolidate, token burn differences, total/10 rounding and cleanup after no coins versus excess burn.', 'Why is the helper not safely replaceable with a call to runCommand using equivalent-looking parameters?')
lesson('multisig','Create, discover and spend coins protected by the fixed root-or-threshold multisignature contract, using custom transaction commands for file workflows.',[
 'Derive the address from the exact contract text. Previous state 1 is an optional root key (0x21 disables it), state 2 the required count, state 3 the key count and states 4 onward the keys. The script first accepts a root signature, otherwise builds and executes a MULTISIG expression.',
 'Create optionally hashes a MiniString ID into state 0, checks root/public-key prefix and string length, and rejects fewer keys than required.getAsInt(). It does not independently require a positive integral threshold or validate every hexadecimal digit at this stage. Delegate funding to send and translate its status/message into the outer reply.',
 'getkey returns the wallet default address’s public key. list searches the contract address and, when id is supplied, matches its hash against every state value rather than only port zero. A coin can appear more than once if several values match.',
 'Spend finds the first matching coin for an id or loads explicit coinid, computes token-scaled change and rejects an equal recipient/source address. It builds txncreate/input/payment commands; positive change copies all old state and emits a state-storing return output. It exports and deletes the temporary row, returning the entire child-result array.',
 'Sign imports a file and checks import status, then examines every state value of the first input for a wallet key. It queues a txnsign for every found key, exports to signed_<original filename> and deletes. Optional vault unlock/relock surrounds execution without finally protection.',
 'Post imports, invokes txnpost mine:true auto:true and deletes. View imports then deletes, returning import details in the child results. Unknown action throws. The accepted mine parameter does not change the hard-coded post mining setting.',
 'Generated command text preserves source quoting and separator behavior. The unused getRequiredFile helper simply resolves file; it does not add validation to these branches.'
], 'Use deterministic contract hashing/state fixtures, including duplicate matching state values and malformed key strings that pass the length check. Record multi-command text, first-input key selection, child-failure propagation and file-name placement. Verify state-preserving change separately from state-free payment. A later VM fixture must test root bypass and threshold satisfaction using real signatures.', 'If the ID hash occurs in two different state ports of one coin, how many entries can list return?')
lesson('multisigread','Expose a reduced multisig command family for key lookup, coin listing, unsigned spend construction and file view/post operations.',[
 'Hash the same fixed root-or-threshold contract text as multisig and generate a random temporary ID before dispatching the requested action.',
 'getkey reads the default wallet public key. list searches the multisig address; optional ID filtering checks all state values and can append duplicate copies of one coin.',
 'Spend resolves an ID to the first matching coin or uses explicit coinid, calculates Minima/token-scaled change and rejects equal source/destination strings. Here address uses getParam, unlike multisig’s getAddressParam normalization.',
 'Build payment with storestate:false. Positive change copies all previous state and emits storestate:true to the original address; export then delete and return all child results.',
 'Post still invokes txnpost mine:true auto:true after import, and view imports/deletes. Thus the READ-oriented name does not mean every branch is side-effect free.',
 'There are no create or sign branches, even though several accepted parameters relate to them. Unknown action throws, and the unused file helper adds no validation.'
], 'Compare shared branches with multisig while explicitly testing Mx versus hex recipient text, duplicate ID-state matches and unknown create/sign actions. Capture imported/deleted rows and the post request with a recording runner. Test permission classification separately; this source alone cannot prove public READ-mode authorization.', 'Why can an Mx spelling of the source address pass this wrapper’s string inequality even when it denotes the same underlying address?')
lesson('send','Select spendable coins, construct proofs and split outputs, sign a transaction and submit it for mining.',[
 'Parse either multi address:amount strings or one recipient, sum amounts and add burn to required Minima funds. Reject negative burn; floor split before checking its configured range. dryrun enables debug; state/storestate/mining/source-address/signkey options are read independently.',
 'Require coinage at least the confirmation depth. Search the current tip for relevant or explicitly addressed token coins and filter by creation height. Scale custom-token requirements into underlying Minima units before selection.',
 'orderCoins sorts the caller’s list descending in place, records first-seen address order, then builds a separate address-grouped result. That grouped result need not remain globally descending. selectCoins skips mining/mempool coins while searching, retains the last sufficient coin until the first insufficient coin, then returns that singleton. If none was found, it returns the entire ordered list, including entries skipped during the scan.',
 'The caller filters mining/mempool entries again and accumulates enough spendable value. Non-simple token scripts or insufficient funds return status:false with a message. Build inputs, choose a proof node using the newest input height capped by MMR proof history, and attach each CoinProof and wallet ScriptProof.',
 'Collect unique signing keys, then apply the explicit signkey override using Java reference inequality against the empty-string literal. This is a source identity quirk, not ordinary string-content comparison. Validate total precision before constructing recipient outputs.',
 'For each recipient divide its underlying amount by split, require a positive share, emit that many outputs and add a positive rounding remainder as an extra output. Positive change first looks up and may validate a default wallet key even if fromaddress later overrides its destination. Change never stores state; output count is checked after construction.',
 'Convert state keys to ports and values through Java string concatenation, precompute output coin IDs and calculate the transaction ID. Outside dryrun, optionally unlock the wallet and sign each required key. Relocking occurs on normal paths and explicit oversize rejection, not in a general finally block.',
 'For token transfers with positive burn, call createBurnTransaction and generate a combined TxPoW; that helper call is outside the dryrun guard. Recalculate its ID and enforce the tip’s byte limit. Non-dryrun submits asynchronously or mines with a 120-second limit; dryrun returns JSON plus detailed byte sizes without this final submission.',
 'The AddressAmount inner class retains recipient data. The demo main prints an orderCoins example; it is not a behavioral parity test.'
], 'First isolate orderCoins/selectCoins with address A values 10 and 1 and address B value 9: grouped order 10,1,9 exposes early termination for required 8. Add mining/mempool flags to show full-list fallback retains skipped entries, and verify caller-list mutation. Then use controlled wallet/tree/miner fixtures for proof height, token precision, fractional split/remainder, repeated keys, dryrun token burn and failure-time relocking. Compare transaction bytes and receiver order, not just a successful reply.', 'For A:10, A:1, B:9 and requirement 8, which single coin is returned? Explain why the algorithm misses the smaller sufficient B coin.')
lesson('sendnosign','Construct an unsigned TxPoW with input proofs and scripts and export it for later offline signing.',[
 'Parse single or multi recipients and total, reject negative burn and accept split between one and twenty without flooring it. Unlike send, dryrun is an accepted but unread parameter.',
 'Move the local tip backward by the confirmation depth, returning status:false if history runs out. Read coinage with default zero even though coinage is absent from getValidParams; normal runner validation and direct calls can differ.',
 'Search relevant unspent coins at that older tip, apply age filtering and reuse send.selectCoins. Filter mining/mempool entries again while accumulating amounts; reject non-simple token scripts or insufficient funds via status:false.',
 'Build inputs and choose an MMR proof node relative to the already-rewound tip, capped by proof history. Attach CoinProofs and wallet ScriptProofs, collecting unique public keys only for logging; no signing loop follows.',
 'Validate total Minima/token precision. Divide each recipient amount by the original split value and loop split.getAsInt() times, always storing state. No extra remainder output is constructed; fractional split and rounding therefore differ from send.',
 'Add positive change to a default wallet address without storing state. State values are cast to String rather than generally stringified. Precompute output IDs and calculate the transaction ID.',
 'For token burn, call createBurnTransaction with its signing Boolean false. Generate/recalculate TxPoW, write the requested file or unsignedtransaction-<time>.txn and return its absolute path. This method does not enforce send’s output-count/TxPoW-size checks or start mining.'
], 'Compare proof-node selection after confirmation rewind, fractional split 1.5, non-divisible amounts, non-string state and the unread dryrun option. Capture the unsigned burn-helper call and file bytes with no miner invocation. Include coinage through direct versus runner calls and ensure codec parity alone is not reported as command parity.', 'With split 1.5, why can the number of outputs and the divisor disagree? Which remainder-handling step is absent?')

def native(name,purpose,steps,adaptation,evidence,exercise):
 author(PREFIX+'sendpoll/'+name+'.md',purpose,steps,adaptation,lambda link:link(CPP/'support/sendpoll.cpp','Read the native polling checks')+'. '+evidence+' These are native assertions, not a Java differential oracle. No test was run while authoring this lesson.',exercise,'The mapped file is partial and parity remains not_verified. The inspected tests have a finite native scope and do not certify full wallet command execution or every thread schedule.')
native('SendPollMessage','Keep a stable queue UID and command string for one retryable send request.',[
 'The one-argument constructor creates sixteen random bytes and stores their 0x string as UID, retaining the supplied command.',
 'The two-argument constructor accepts the supplied UID and command, including null; it generates no replacement identity.',
 'toJSON writes uid followed by command, preserving nulls and JSON escaping.',
 'copy creates a separate message with the same two string references/values. Copying a queue snapshot does not assign new UIDs.'
], 'C++ uses optional strings to represent Java null and value copies to preserve immutable string semantics. It reuses MiniData random generation and actual JSONObject rendering; independent entropy is not expected to match byte for byte.', 'The harness checks exact null JSON, escaped Unicode command copy equality, sixteen-byte UID width and uniqueness among 1000 samples. This sample uniqueness check does not prove collision impossibility or Java entropy equivalence.', 'Why must copying a retry entry preserve its UID?')
native('SendPollManager','Retry queued commands periodically, remove successful entries and retain failures for a later poll.',[
 'Construction schedules SENDPOLL_FUNCTION after the mutable default thirty seconds. SENDPOLL_LIST and SENDPOLL_CLEAR have transposed string values, and neither has a handling branch.',
 'Add creates a new SendPollMessage under the queue lock. listCommands creates copied messages; removeCommand constructs a replacement list omitting every matching UID.',
 'On SENDPOLL_FUNCTION, iterate a copied snapshot and check isRunning before each entry. New commands inserted while processing wait for a later snapshot.',
 'Run each command through CommandRunner, cast status to Boolean and remove it only for true. Sleep one second after every normally completed attempt, including success.',
 'After the loop schedule another poll, even when stopping broke the loop. An exception in runner/status/sleep escapes before that final schedule; no retry timer is posted by this method on that path.',
 'Unknown message types do nothing; null message/type fails. Removing a null requested UID normally matches no generated UID, while a null stored UID fails when equality is called.'
], 'C++ reuses MessageProcessor, TimerMessage and SendPollMessage with a mutex-protected vector and atomic delay. Factory creation establishes ownership before scheduling/starting the worker. A required command runner callback and overridable timing seams allow controlled tests; binding it to actual wallet commands remains a separate integration step.', 'The harness records success/retry removal, detached snapshots, a reentrant insertion, missing-status failure before pause/reschedule, stop during polling, null/unknown types and 1000 concurrent additions/removals. One native worker/timer experiment invokes only a controlled offline callback and checks release/join cleanup. It does not send funds or compare Java scheduling.', 'If a command result omits status, does the next poll get scheduled by this function? Identify the exact exception boundary.')

# Verified command/manager integration supersedes the initial source-only lesson.
author(PREFIX+'send/sendpoll.md',
 'Manage retryable command text through add, list and remove; actual execution belongs to the polling worker.',[
 'Read action, defaulting to add, then obtain Main’s manager before testing any action branch.',
 'For add, replace only the first case-sensitive sendpoll occurrence in the complete command text. Reject only exact send. Empty direct-call text is accepted.',
 'Add the text through the existing locked manager. Return response.command without executing or validating a transaction.',
 'For list, turn the copied message list into response.commands and count total. For remove, require uid and report it even when absent from the queue.',
 'An unknown action returns an empty response, although the Main lookup still occurs. A null manager only fails if the chosen branch dereferences it.'
 ],
 'The C++ wrapper reuses SendPollManager, SendPollMessage, Command and CommandRunner. The fixed literal replacement uses find/replace once. An explicit getManager binding stands in for the unfinished native Main owner; its default throws a typed null-receiver exception. The manager is dereferenced after branch-specific parameter validation, matching source order.',
 lambda link:link(CPP/'tools/sendpoll_command_differential.py','Read the Java/C++ comparison')+' and '+link(CPP/'student-guide/new-tests/send-polling-command.md','the lab')+' cover 367 programs and 3,216 operations in both normal and ASAN/UBSAN builds. Compare exact metadata, queue contents, detached snapshots, removal, errors and public runner dispatch. Actual worker processing removes a successful hash command and retains a failed command. Stopping keeps queued work but still schedules a timer. Random UIDs are shape-checked and consistently renamed; NPE/CCE types are compared while runtime prose is normalized.',
 'Why does action:unknown fail when Main is missing, yet succeed when Main exists with a null polling manager?',
 'The counterpart is implemented_partial and parity remains not_verified. The fixture does not start Main, deliver background timers or compare logger output. Generic C++ cast prose differs from Java class/loader details. Existing worker tests cover additional native concurrency behavior; full runtime, storage and exhaustive scheduling remain unfinished.')
